      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Engagement Hub Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Applications will be accepted until 11:59PM EST on the posting closing date. To apply, please complete the online application available at https://jobs.uncw.edu/ and attach the following materials as Adobe PDF documents: Cover Letter addressed to Search Committee Chair Mark Sorensen Curriculum Vita Teaching Philosophy Additional materials may be requested from applicants invited to interview for the position. Please note that a minimum of three references are required for all applications. The reference contact information you provide may be used to request reference letters during the screening process. Letters of application without the requested components will not meet the application requirements. Questions about the position or the online application process should be directed to CHSSA Recruitment Specialist Jennifer Itell @ itellj@uncw.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40911 College College of Humanities, Social Sciences, and The Arts - 321 College Dept/School Theatre - 32122 Vacancy Number 16F-799 Position Number 3584 Location of Workplace Main UNCW Campus Brief Summary of Work for this Position The Department of Theatre at the University of North Carolina Wilmington invites applications for a tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies to begin August 2027. Teaching responsibilities may include courses in dramatic literature, performance studies, theatre history, introductory theatre courses, and courses related to the candidate’s scholarly and creative expertise. In addition to a full teaching load, the successful candidate will be expected to serve on both departmental and university committees as well as maintain an active publishing and/or creative scholarly agenda. We particularly welcome candidates who can articulate their approach to pedagogy and demonstrate an ongoing investment in developing their teaching. The area of specialization is open. We’re seeking someone whose work complements existing faculty strengths and expands the intellectual and artistic breadth of the program. Research may draw upon a range of historical periods, geographic and cultural contexts, methodologies, theatrical forms, or interdisciplinary approaches to theatre studies. The successful candidate will be an active participant in the intellectual, creative, and organizational life of a future-looking department. We seek a colleague who values collaborating and contributing to the long-term development of the theatre program. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Ph.D. or DFA in Theatre or Performance Studies at the time of application Experience teaching at the university level Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and mentorship Demonstrated potential for significant scholarly productivity Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills & Experience Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate a clear pedagogical approach and an ongoing investment in developing their teaching whose work complements existing faculty strengths and expands the intellectual and artistic breadth of the program Required Certifications or Licensure Primary Function of Organizational Unit The UNCW Department of Theatre provides high-quality education in the study and practice of theatre within a liberal arts environment. We combine pre-professional training with a solid academic core to prepare our students for numerous career pathways in theatre, film, and other related disciplines. We provide students a range of production opportunities to enhance their knowledge and love of the artform and offer outreach programs designed to serve both the university community and the greater Wilmington area. College/School Information The College of Humanities, Social Sciences, and the Arts ( CHSSA ) is home to 14 academic departments and offers a wide variety of undergraduate and graduate degree programs including the Bachelor of Arts, Bachelor of Fine Arts, Bachelor of Music, Master of Arts, Master of Fine Arts, and Master of Public Administration as well as combined bachelor’s/master’s degree programs in Spanish and English. The CHSSA also houses the Gender Studies and Research Center and the Academic Resource Center, which offers full-service, professional advising for all CHSSA undergraduate students. In addition, the CHSSA offers a full complement of interdisciplinary minors and post baccalaureate certificates including: Africana studies, American studies, Asian studies, classical studies, conflict management and resolution, emergency and disaster management, forensic science, Hispanic studies, journalism, Latin American studies, medical humanities, Middle East and Islamic studies, Native American studies, professional writing and publishing, science and medical writing, and women’s, gender, and sexuality studies. The CHSSA contributes significantly to the curriculum that comprises UNCW’s University Studies Program, through which all undergraduates gain a foundation in the liberal arts and develop the transferable skills essential for life in the twenty-first century. The CHSSA strives in its undergraduate programs and in its University Study offerings to nurture creative thinking, intellectual curiosity, and academic integrity in students while providing them with a solid foundation of knowledge in their chosen fields. Graduate programs in the CHSSA are designed to develop intellectual competence and to prepare the student for careers in business, industry, government, teaching or for further study at the doctoral level. Applied learning is a hallmark of the student experience in the College of Humanities, Social Sciences, and the Arts. Each of the CHSSA’s departments requires an applied learning experience as a part of the curriculum for its undergraduate majors. Examples include faculty-directed research, internships, service learning, and capstone courses and projects, all of which challenge students to integrate various strands of knowledge and to apply that knowledge to broader, real-world or real disciplinary situations. Upon completion of their studies, all CHSSA students will have the necessary preparation for rewarding careers, advanced study, effective citizenship, and meaningful lives. The College of Humanities, Social Science, and the Arts offers limitless opportunities to engage in collaborative and interdisciplinary research and service while also making a positive societal impact. Come and join our vibrant academic environment that values discovery, innovation, and creativity. University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research, and service. UNCW is distinguished by its commitment to putting students first, supporting world-class faculty and staff, delivering transformative learning experiences, and leveraging its unique proximity to the ocean. Recognized nationally for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking and reflects emerging industries and interdisciplinary innovation. A public institution with more than 20,500 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s first bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Founded as Wilmington College in 1947, UNCW moved to its present location in the heart of New Hanover County in 1961. The 660-acre campus is only minutes from Wrightsville Beach and historic downtown Wilmington and features Georgian architecture and designated conservation areas. Wilmington International Airport ( ILM ) provides commercial air service to cities both domestic and abroad and is just six miles from the UNCW campus. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Number of Openings Single Incumbent Special Notes to Applicants Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Applications will be accepted until 11:59PM EST on the posting closing date. To apply, please complete the online application available at https://jobs.uncw.edu/ and attach the following materials as Adobe PDF documents: Cover Letter addressed to Search Committee Chair Mark Sorensen Curriculum Vita Teaching Philosophy Additional materials may be requested from applicants invited to interview for the position. Please note that a minimum of three references are required for all applications. The reference contact information you provide may be used to request reference letters during the screening process. Letters of application without the requested components will not meet the application requirements. Questions about the position or the online application process should be directed to CHSSA Recruitment Specialist Jennifer Itell @ itellj@uncw.edu . Position Type Permanent Job Posting Date 09/30/2026 Job Close Date 11/02/2026 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity with UNCW? (2026) UNCW Website UNCW LinkedIn Page UNCW X Account (formerly Twitter) UNCW Employee Referral UNCW Instagram Account (UNCW_jobs) UNCW Job Alert Chronical of Higher Education Glassdoor Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed North Carolina Job Network Craigslist Career Events/Job Fairs Billboards/Marquee Other If you responded \"other\" above, please indicate where you learned of the faculty opportunity at UNCW: (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
