    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/41351": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar – Economics of Coastal Hazards and Resilience",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Postdoctoral Scholar – Economics of Coastal Hazards and Resilience Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Engagement Hub Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Postdoctoral Scholar – Economics of Coastal Hazards and Resilience Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note, this is a postdoctoral position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need, with the possibility of continuation. Employees in postdoc positions are considered temporary positions (non-permanent state employees) but do qualify for postdoctoral medical insurance and paid leave, unlike other temporary employees at the university. More information about postdoctoral employees can be found in the Postdoc Handbook. To receive consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you apply for this position. For more info/to apply, visit the applicant portal . Applications must be submitted through the online application system by 11:59 pm EST of the posting close date to be considered. Posting Details Posting Details Vacancy Number PD-0035 Working Title Postdoctoral Scholar – Economics of Coastal Hazards and Resilience Position Number PD0038 Location of Workplace Main UNCW Campus Brief Summary of Work for this Position The Cameron School of Business at the University of North Carolina Wilmington invites applications for a postdoctoral scholar in the Department of Economics and Finance. This is a 12-month, full-time, temporary non-faculty research position, with potential renewal subject to university policies and available funding. The postdoctoral scholar will work with Professor Meghan Millea on the economics research thrust of the National Science Foundation-funded Coastal Hazards, Economic Prosperity, and Resilience ( CHEER ) research hub. CHEER brings together engineers, economists, and social scientists to investigate hurricane risk, recovery, and resilience in coastal communities. The economics thrust examines household and community responses to hurricane risk, including insurance decisions, hazard mitigation, adaptation, and the economic consequences of disasters, with an emphasis on eastern North Carolina. The primary responsibility of the postdoctoral scholar is to conduct research. Activities include developing and applying quantitative economic methods, assembling and analyzing data, interpreting results, preparing manuscripts and presentations, and collaborating with researchers across institutions and disciplines. The position may also involve research proposal development, mentoring students, and engaging with community partners to connect research findings with practical needs. Appointment Description This is a 12-month, full-time, temporary non-faculty research position, with potential renewal subject to university policies and available funding. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Ph.D. in Economics, Applied Economics, Environmental or Resource Economics, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in one of the fields listed above and conferred before the appointment start date, but no more than five (5) years prior to the appointment start date. Exceptions to the 5-year degree requirement may be waived in exceptional circumstances. Research experience in applied quantitative analysis, including econometric or computational methods. Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and communicate findings in writing and presentations. Ability to collaborate on interdisciplinary research projects. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills & Experience Research experience in environmental economics, natural hazards, disaster risk, insurance, adaptation, or economic resilience. Experience with spatial analysis, applied econometrics, economic modeling, or computable general equilibrium methods. Experience working with large or geographically detailed datasets and collaborating with researchers from other disciplines. Record of scholarly publications or manuscripts in progress and interest in research that informs policy and community decision-making. Required Certifications or Licensure Department Economics and Finance - 31250 Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Economics and Finance at the University of North Carolina Wilmington, located in the vibrant coastal city of Wilmington, North Carolina, offers four Bachelor of Science in Business Administration concentrations: Economics, Finance, Financial Technology (FinTech), and Real Estate. The department also administers the Bachelor of Arts in Economics and the Master of Science in Finance programs. In addition, faculty play an integral role in supporting both the Master of Business Administration ( MBA ) and the International MBA , a joint program offered in collaboration with our international partner universities. The department fosters an engaging and experiential learning environment through student organizations, competitive academic opportunities such as the College Fed Challenge and CFA Institute Research Challenge, the student-managed investment fund, undergraduate honors research, and other high-impact learning experiences. Faculty are equally committed to advancing scholarship with a growing research portfolio and a strong culture of collaboration that enhances teaching, research, and service. College Cameron School Business - 312 College College/School Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington ( UNCW ) is a dynamic and growing institution within the University of North Carolina System, set on a scenic, 661-acre campus. The AACSB -accredited Cameron School of Business offers a broad range of undergraduate and graduate programs across business and technology disciplines, including management, accounting, analytics, finance, supply chain management, marketing, economics, entrepreneurship, cybersecurity, and information systems. Located in Wilmington, a vibrant coastal city with a thriving port, diverse business community, and strong tourism industry, UNCW offers a distinctive setting for academic and professional growth. Bordered by the Atlantic Ocean and the Cape Fear River, Wilmington combines a robust economic environment with an appealing coastal quality of life. University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Please note, this is a postdoctoral position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need, with the possibility of continuation. Employees in postdoc positions are considered temporary positions (non-permanent state employees) but do qualify for postdoctoral medical insurance and paid leave, unlike other temporary employees at the university. More information about postdoctoral employees can be found in the Postdoc Handbook. To receive consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you apply for this position. For more info/to apply, visit the applicant portal . Applications must be submitted through the online application system by 11:59 pm EST of the posting close date to be considered. Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Number of Openings 12J (12 Months: July - June/Salary) Special Notes to Applicants Please note, this is a postdoctoral position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need, with the possibility of continuation. Employees in postdoc positions are considered temporary positions (non-permanent state employees) but do qualify for postdoctoral medical insurance and paid leave, unlike other temporary employees at the university. More information about postdoctoral employees can be found in the Postdoc Handbook. To receive consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you apply for this position. For more info/to apply, visit the applicant portal . Applications must be submitted through the online application system by 11:59 pm EST of the posting close date to be considered. Requested Job Posting Date 10/30/2026 Posting Close Date 11/09/2026 Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/41180 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita List of 3 Professional References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this postdoc opportunity with UNCW? UNCW or College Website Direct Contact from UNCW Faculty or Staff Professional Organization or Association Listserv or Professional Job Board UNCW Social Media Higher Ed Publication (such as Chronicle of Higher Education, Inside Higher Ed, Higher Ed Jobs) HERC (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) Postdoc Specific Website/Job Search (careers.nationalpostdoc.org; postdocjobs.com; etc.) Other If you responded \"other\" above, please indicate where you learned of the postdoctoral opportunity at UNCW: (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/41340": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Track, School of Nursing",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Clinical Track, School of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Engagement Hub Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Open Rank Clinical Track, School of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate(s) selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Open Rank Clinical Track, School of Nursing External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/41334 College College of Health and Human Services - 315 College Dept/School School of Nursing - 31510 Vacancy Number 16F-829 Position Number 4189 Location of Workplace Main UNCW Campus Brief Summary of Work for this Position The School of Nursing ( SON ), within the College of Health and Human Services ( CHHS ) at the University of North Carolina Wilmington ( UNCW ) invites applications for full-time, 9-month clinical track faculty at the rank of Clinical Instructor, Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor starting August 2027. Clinical track faculty may be hired on a contract of up to 5 years that is renewable based on performance. Clinical track faculty are eligible for promotion to higher clinical track ranks. Appointment to rank is dependent on qualifications relative to the university, college, and school standards. The primary teaching responsibilities will be assigned across the undergraduate and graduate nursing programs based on teaching and clinical experience. In addition, clinical track faculty have expectations related to advising/mentoring students, scholarship, performing professional and community service and outreach, and contributing to ongoing program evaluation and improvement depending on their rank. Faculty are required to have a presence on campus. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements A master’s degree in nursing OR doctoral degree in nursing OR a doctorate in a related discipline with a baccalaureate OR a graduate degree in nursing. Appointment at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor requires evidence of successful teaching experience appropriate to the rank. Note: Applicants with earned doctoral degrees will be given preference. If ABD at time of application, all degree requirements must be completed and the terminal degree officially conferred prior to the start of the appointment. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills & Experience Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience and clinical expertise in adult health, psych/mental health, or maternity. Experience with AI use in educational and professional settings Required Certifications or Licensure A current RN license in NC or eligibility for licensure in NC for all nursing programs. To teach in the DNP program, certification in specialty Primary Function of Organizational Unit The School of Nursing ( SON ) within the College of Health and Human Services ( CHHS ) at the University of North Carolina Wilmington ( UNCW ) has an outstanding legacy of serving the people of southeastern North Carolina through education, research/scholarship, and service. The SON is dedicated to excellence in the development of healthcare professionals through in-depth education, professional partnerships, applied research, regional engagement, and community outreach and impact. Nursing programs in the SON are CCNE accredited and the SON has been recognized by the National League of Nursing as a Center of Excellence in Nursing Education, specifically in the area of promoting the pedagogical expertise of faculty. The SON is located in McNeill Hall, a state-of-the-art facility that includes offices, classrooms, a large lecture hall, computer laboratories, student success areas and learning commons, and the Simulation Learning Center. The Simulation Learning Center uses high, medium, and low-fidelity human patient simulators as teaching and learning tools for nursing education. Through the use of simulation, we strive to create a realistic environment and a powerful learning experience that promotes the cognitive, affective, physical, and social development of the student as well as the incorporation of inter-professional collaborative experiences for students across the degree programs in the College. The SON offers the following degree and certificate programs: Nursing BS in Nursing (Prelicensure, RN- BSN , Accelerated) MS in Nursing (Nurse Educator) Nurse Educator Certificate DNP / BSN to DNP (Family Nurse Practitioner, Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner, Adult-Gero Nurse Practitioner) MSN to DNP (Nurse Executive Leadership and Post- APRN concentrations) Clinical Research BS in Clinical Research Post- Baccalaureate Certificate in Clinical Research Operations MS in Clinical Research and Product Development Over 2,400 students are enrolled in programs within the SON . The SON has 88 full-time faculty and employs over 70 temp. faculty per semester College/School Information The College of Health and Human Services was created in July 2010 to provide UNCW with a new mechanism to link and focus its health-related research, professional continuing education, and health knowledge dissemination and application. In the formative stage of development, the CHHS is currently home to three professional schools: School of Health and Applied Human Sciences, School of Nursing, and School of Social Work. This is an outstanding opportunity to join a dynamic College that seeks to be nationally recognized for its inter-professional collaboration, community engagement and impact, and implementation science. The faculty, staff and students of the CHHS are committed to the pursuit of excellence and enhancing health and quality of life across the lifespan for individuals, families and communities in southeastern North Carolina and beyond. University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Number of Openings Special Notes to Applicants Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate(s) selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Position Type Permanent Job Posting Date 10/30/2026 Job Close Date 11/30/2026 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vita List of 3 Professional References Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this faculty opportunity with UNCW? *UNCW or College Website *Direct Contact from UNCW Faculty or Staff *Professional Organization or Association *Listserv or Professional Job Board *UNCW Social Media *Higher Ed Publication (such as Chronicle of Higher *Education, Inside Higher Ed, Higher Ed Jobs) *HERC (Higher Education Recruitment Consortium) *Other (Open Ended Question) If you responded \"other\" above, please indicate where you learned of the faculty opportunity at UNCW: (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
